    "blocks": [
      {
        "id": "p1",
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": "You were walking next to a swimming pool. "
          },
          {
            "t": "blank",
            "id": "b1",
            "number": 1
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": ", you "
          },
          {
            "t": "vocab",
            "v": "slipped",
            "ref": "v-slip"
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": " and dropped your phone into the water. Or it slipped out of your hand when you were next to a toilet."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "p2",
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": "However, your smartphone got wet, so you now need to "
          },
          {
            "t": "blank",
            "id": "b2",
            "number": 2
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": " it. But what do you do? Probably, you remember your friends’ suggestion: Put it in a bag of rice. The rice can "
          },
          {
            "t": "blank",
            "id": "b3",
            "number": 3
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": " any remaining water from the smartphone. This saves its "
          },
          {
            "t": "gloss",
            "v": "circuitry",
            "zh": "电路"
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": " in the process. They promised that this would certainly work. What is there to lose?"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "p3",
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": "However, Apple warns that putting your wet smartphone into rice to dry is not a good idea. It could "
          },
          {
            "t": "blank",
            "id": "b4",
            "number": 4
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": " cause even more problems."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "p4",
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": "“Don’t put your iPhone in a bag of rice,” Apple says on its support site. “Doing so could damage your iPhone.” Tiny pieces of rice could get into the "
          },
          {
            "t": "vocab",
            "v": "crevices",
            "ref": "v-crevice"
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": " of your phone and do "
          },
          {
            "t": "blank",
            "id": "b5",
            "number": 5
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": " to it. Besides, rice simply isn’t as effective as other drying "
          },
          {
            "t": "blank",
            "id": "b6",
            "number": 6
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": ", such as "
          },
          {
            "t": "gloss",
            "v": "silica packets",
            "zh": "二氧化硅包"
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": "."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "p5",
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": "In case of a wet iPhone, the company also advises users not to use an “"
          },
          {
            "t": "vocab",
            "v": "external",
            "ref": "v-external"
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": " heat source” such as a blow dryer. Trying to put napkins and paper towels into "
          },
          {
            "t": "gloss",
            "v": "charging ports",
            "zh": "充电口"
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": " could make things "
          },
          {
            "t": "blank",
            "id": "b7",
            "number": 7
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": " as well. Instead, Apple says, try to tap the device against your hand “with the connector facing down” to shake the water out. Then let the phone dry out in a place with some "
          },
          {
            "t": "blank",
            "id": "b8",
            "number": 8
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": " (perhaps with a fan) for at least 30 minutes. From there, try connecting it to a "
          },
          {
            "t": "gloss",
            "v": "cable charger",
            "zh": "充电器连接线"
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": "."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "p6",
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": "“If your phone has dried out but still isn’t charging, remove the cable and then "
          },
          {
            "t": "blank",
            "id": "b9",
            "number": 9
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": " it again,” says Apple."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "p7",
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": "What if it’s seawater or a drink? Put the phone in clean water for a few minutes before drying it out. This is to "
          },
          {
            "t": "blank",
            "id": "b10",
            "number": 10
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": " any "
          },
          {
            "t": "gloss",
            "v": "impurities",
            "zh": "杂质"
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": " that could speed up "
          },
          {
            "t": "vocab",
            "v": "corrosion",
            "ref": "v-corrosion"
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": " of the circuitry inside."
          }
        ]
      }
    ]
  },
